Run all 25 SPEC CPU2006 benchmarks in parallel.

The original script sets the number of parallel simulations P to
min(physical cores, RAM / 2 GiB). On the 2 x 14-core node used here P was
fixed to 25, so that every benchmark runs at once on its own physical core.
Change P to suit your machine.

Applies to: scripts/run_spec06.sh (artefact tag AEV3)

diff --git a/scripts/run_spec06.sh b/scripts/run_spec06.sh
index 24c6d39..a532f20 100755
--- a/scripts/run_spec06.sh
+++ b/scripts/run_spec06.sh
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@ cd SPEC/benchspec/CPU2006/
 N=$(grep ^cpu\\scores /proc/cpuinfo | uniq |  awk '{print $4}')
 M=$(grep MemTotal /proc/meminfo | awk '{print $2}')
 G=$(expr $M / 2097152)
-P=$((G<N ? G : N))
+P=25
 i=0
 for bench in xalancbmk cactusADM zeusmp astar bwaves bzip2  calculix gamess gcc GemsFDTD gobmk gromacs h264ref hmmer lbm leslie3d libquantum  milc namd omnetpp povray sjeng soplex tonto mcf
 do
